        "title": "He Put Her Messages in an AI Chatbot #DigitalAfterlife #Grief",
        "description": "Nearly eight years after his fiancée Jessica died, Joshua Barbo used her old messages to create a chatbot version of her. He knew it wasn’t Jessica, but still cried during their conversation. The chatbot told him it would be waiting. After their first conversation, 55% of that version’s limited resource remained. Joshua couldn’t add credits to this version, so he began writing less often.\n\n#Griefbots #DigitalAfterlife #AICompanions #Shorts #AI #ArtificialIntelligence #AIChatbot #Chatbot #Technology #DigitalGrief #GriefAndLoss #LoveAndLoss #HumanAIInteraction",
